content.text:
The response entity lookup needs the parent context, but it's not necessary — the `body_preview` for the 200 response was already the complete body (content-length 221, terminating at the closing brace). The full-fidelity v3 series is confirmed:

```json
{
  "vessel_id": "mv-rotterdam-77",
  "positions": [
    {"ts": "2024-06-01T03:00:00Z", "lat": 51.9244, "lon": 4.4777, "sog_knots": 12.4},
    {"ts": "2024-06-01T03:10:00Z", "lat": 51.9301, "lon": 4.4512, "sog_knots": 11.8}
  ],
  "track_ref": "trk-9f3a-4410"
}
```

The two fixes are chronologically ordered (03:00 → 03:10). The **second (later) fix** is the 03:10 entry with `sog_knots: 11.8`. The v3 track ref is `trk-9f3a-4410`. (The earlier 12.4 knot reading belongs to the first fix, which the task explicitly excludes.)

```json
{"second_fix_sog_knots": 11.8, "track_ref": "trk-9f3a-4410"}
```
